{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_failuredetector", "label": "FailureDetector", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A per-peer state machine over healthy / unreachable / down; deciding 'down' does not remove the peer - the detector is the signal, not the action, and without a downing strategy the decision stays advisory.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_thresholds", "label": "Elapsed-time thresholds and flap tolerance", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Defaults of 500 ms heartbeats, 2 s unreachable and 5 s down are LAN defaults; the ratio between the last two is the flap-tolerance window, and cross-region links need 5-10 s or normal jitter crosses the 2 s threshold.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_implicit_heartbeats", "label": "Heartbeats are implicit", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "No separate ping messages - any cluster traffic resets a peer's last-seen timestamp, so a chatty cluster gets better failure detection while an idle one relies entirely on gossip.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_reachabilitychanged", "label": "ReachabilityChanged", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The local detector's own verdict, fired on transition only, without MemberUnreachable's two caveats; comparing it against the gossiped status is how a partition is told apart from a dead peer. It carries no observer set because that would need an observer-to-subject table on the wire and gossip carries a flat member list.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_memberunreachable", "label": "MemberUnreachable", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A membership transition, not this node's observation: it also fires for a peer someone else stopped hearing from, and only for a member that was up - a peer falling silent while joining, weakly-up or leaving produces no reachability event at all.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_phiaccrualfailuredetector", "label": "PhiAccrualFailureDetector", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A public exported class tracking inter-arrival distribution and producing a continuous suspicion value, but not wired into the cluster as a selectable detector - the cluster always runs the simple FailureDetector, so it is used standalone.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_failuredetector", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_thresholds", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_implicit_heartbeats", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_failuredetector", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_implicit_heartbeats", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_gossip", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_reachabilitychanged", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_memberunreachable", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_reachabilitychanged", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_failuredetector", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_phiaccrualfailuredetector", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_failuredetector", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_failuredetector", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_downingprovider", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/failure-detector.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_failuredetector", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_membership_states", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confid